.TH FERDIM-DBUS 1 "2026-11-24" "ferdim 1.10.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ferdim-dbus \- D-Bus bridge for the FerDim download manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ferdim-dbus
.SH DESCRIPTION
Optional session-bus service that owns the name
.B org.ferdim.Daemon
and exports the object
.I /org/ferdim/Daemon
with the interface
.BR org.ferdim.Daemon1 :
methods \fBAdd\fR(url), \fBPause\fR(id), \fBResume\fR(id), \fBCancel\fR(id),
\fBList\fR() and \fBStats\fR() (both return JSON), \fBWebUrl\fR() (returns a
single-use web UI address), the \fBVersion\fR property
and the \fBChanged\fR(json) signal. It forwards every call to the
.BR ferdim (1)
daemon over its local socket. D-Bus activation starts the bridge on demand;
desktop shells and the bundled GNOME Shell extension use it. Requires
PyGObject (Gio).
.SH FILES
/usr/share/dbus-1/services/org.ferdim.Daemon.service
.br
/usr/share/dbus-1/interfaces/org.ferdim.Daemon1.xml
.SH EXAMPLES
gdbus call \-\-session \-\-dest org.ferdim.Daemon \-\-object\-path
/org/ferdim/Daemon \-\-method org.ferdim.Daemon1.Stats
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ferdim (1),
.BR gdbus (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Enes Aksu <eaksu@pm.me>
